    "final_text": "I fixed the bug: `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`. The full test suite passes (9 of 9), and the two new tests fail on the old code.\n\n**Root cause:** the query serializer in `src/url-builder.js` skipped any value that counts as \"false-like\" in JavaScript. That check was meant to drop missing values, but it also dropped `0` and `false`:\n- in `serializeQuery()`, top-level query values were skipped with `if (!value)`\n- in `appendQueryValue()`, array items were skipped with `if (!item)`\n\nArrays were affected too, which the issue doesn't mention: `attempt: [0, 1]` came out as just `attempt=1`.\n\n**Fix:** both checks now use a small helper, `isOmittedQueryValue()`, which skips only `undefined`, `null` and `''`. Numbers and booleans are now always kept. The issue's example now builds `https://api.example.test/webhooks/deliveries?dry_run=true&include_archived=false&retry=0`. I didn't change the API or any other code.\n\n**Regression tests** (in `tests/url-builder.test.js`):\n- `buildUrl keeps numeric zero and boolean false query values (ISSUE-214)` runs the exact call from the issue.\n- `serializeQuery keeps zero and false array items but omits missing values` covers `0` and `false` inside arrays, and checks that `null`, `undefined` and `''` are still left out.\n\nBefore the fix, both failed with the exact output the issue reports (`...?dry_run=true`).\n\n`ISSUE.md` now has a `Resolution` section naming the fixed functions and the two tests.\n\n**Decision for you:** I chose to keep dropping empty strings (`''`) as before, since the issue only covers `0` and `false`. If you want `key=` sent for empty strings, remove `value === ''` from the helper, but that changes behavior for anyone who relies on empty values being left out. One minor side effect: `NaN` used to be dropped and would now be sent as `NaN`.",
